@startuml sequence-wallets-transactions
title individuals-api - wallets and transactions through transaction-service

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor Client
participant "SecurityConfig" as Sec
participant "WalletController /\nTransactionController" as Ctl
participant "WalletService /\nTransactionService" as Svc
participant "TransactionClient" as TCl
participant "transaction-service" as Tx
participant "Keycloak" as Kc

Client -> Sec : any of the 11 operations, e.g.\nPOST /api/v1/transactions/withdrawal/confirm\nAuthorization: Bearer token
Sec -> Kc : JWKS (signing keys, cached)
alt no token, expired or bad signature
  Sec --> Client : 401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED
  note right of Sec : transaction-service is not called
end

Sec -> Ctl : request + verified Jwt
alt @Valid fails: required fields, uuid, amount > 0, page / size,\nthe two wallets of a transfer (@DifferentWallets on the client's class)
  Ctl --> Client : 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
end

Ctl -> Svc : request, Jwt
Svc -> Svc : KeycloakClaims.requireUserUid(jwt)
alt the token carries no user_uid (realm mapper broken)
  Svc --> Client : 500 INTERNAL_ERROR
end

Svc -> TCl : user_uid, request
TCl -> Tx : same path and body + X-User-Uid: user_uid\nWalletsApi / TransactionsApi on transactionWebClient
note right of TCl
  The client never sends user_uid:
  GET /api/v1/wallets -> GET /api/v1/wallets/user/{user_uid}
  GET /api/v1/transactions?... -> ...&userUid=user_uid
end note

alt 2xx
  Tx --> TCl : 200 / 201 + body
  TCl --> Svc : the body (client class)
  Svc --> Ctl : the body
  Ctl --> Client : same status, same body
else 400 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS, CURRENCY_MISMATCH,\nWALLET_NOT_ACTIVE, WALLET_TYPE_NOT_ACTIVE
  Tx --> TCl : 400 + error code
  TCl --> Client : 400, the same error code
else 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (their rules caught\nwhat ours let through)
  Tx --> TCl : 400 VALIDATION_ERROR + details
  TCl --> Client : 400 VALIDATION_ERROR, their details
else 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST or an unknown error code
  Tx --> TCl : 400
  TCl --> Client : 500 INTERNAL_ERROR, their body only in the log (our bug)
else 404 WALLET_NOT_FOUND, WALLET_TYPE_NOT_FOUND,\nTRANSACTION_NOT_FOUND
  Tx --> TCl : 404 + error code
  TCl --> Client : 404, the same error code
  note right of TCl : another user's wallet is 404 too:\ntransaction-service looks only among\nthe wallets of this user_uid
else 409 REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT
  Tx --> TCl : 409
  TCl --> Client : 409 REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT
else 5xx
  Tx --> TCl : 5xx
  TCl --> Client : 503 DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE
else no connection or no answer within responseTimeout (5 s)
  TCl --> Client : 503 DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE
end

note over Client, Tx
  Errors travel as ApiException to GlobalExceptionHandler and leave
  as our ErrorResponseDto (timestamp, path, status, error, message,
  traceId, details), not as transaction-service's problem details.

  Timeout on confirm: the operation may have been committed. The client
  repeats confirm with the same requestId: transaction-service answers 200
  with the transaction it already made and never charges twice.
  individuals-api does not repeat the call itself.

  individuals-api has no database: wallets and transactions are written
  by transaction-service only (its own sequence diagrams).
end note

@enduml
